  "milestone_brief": "### desktop-distribution-spike-1 \u2014 Prove a relocatable bundled sidecar\n\n**Question.** Can the installed arXMCP wheel, operator-console assets, native libraries, and model-loading path run as a relocatable macOS sidecar without ambient Python or a repository checkout?\n\n**Timebox.** At most 3 days. The output is a disposable bundle, evidence, and an ADR\u2014not production packaging.\n\n**Acceptance criteria.**\n- Build a disposable one-directory sidecar from pinned inputs and launch it from an arbitrary read-only path on a supported Apple Silicon Mac.\n- Start in bootstrap mode, reach /healthz, locate packaged templates/static assets, and exercise the model-loading import path without a repository checkout.\n- Record artifact size, cold startup, native-library closure, codesigning implications, and any dependency that cannot be relocated.\n- Compare the leading bundling modes and record GO/NO-GO plus fallback in an ADR.\n- Do not commit models, credentials, or generated binaries.\n\n**Dependencies.** None.\n\n**GitHub issue.** chris-dare-dev/arXMCP#384.",
  "brief_source": "legacy-prose plans/desktop-distribution-roadmap.md:167; GitHub #384",
